    "text": "Light wave travelling in air along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-direction is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>540</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Then, the peak value of magnetic field of wave will be (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
